Subject: [PW3] Product option: software Canvas for all application windows

PW3 has no GPU. With CPU-emulated OpenGL ES every hwui frame is rasterized
by a software GLES implementation on one Cortex-A9 core. The existing
framework switch that persistent low-RAM processes already use selects the
software Canvas renderer instead. The upstream default is unchanged: the
option is off unless the product sets ro.pw3.software_canvas.

Rebased on 2026-10-29: this used to sit after the per-package diagnostic
switch (patch 0005), which went with the rest of the debug chain, so its
context is now the line the diagnostic used to follow.

--- a/core/java/android/app/ActivityThread.java
+++ b/core/java/android/app/ActivityThread.java
@@ -5437,6 +5437,15 @@
         Process.setStartTimes(SystemClock.elapsedRealtime(), SystemClock.uptimeMillis());
 
         mBoundApplication = data;
+        // PW3 product policy: the device has no GPU, so OpenGL ES is emulated on
+        // its single CPU core and the software Canvas renderer is the faster path
+        // for every application window. Decided before the process creates a
+        // window; debug.pw3.software_canvas overrides the product default for
+        // processes started afterwards.
+        if (SystemProperties.getBoolean("debug.pw3.software_canvas",
+                SystemProperties.getBoolean("ro.pw3.software_canvas", false))) {
+            ThreadedRenderer.disable(false);
+        }
         mConfiguration = new Configuration(data.config);
         mCompatConfiguration = new Configuration(data.config);
 
